  "Question": "Jack had a bag of \\(128\\) apples. He sold \\(25\\%\\) of them to Jill. Next he sold \\(25\\%\\) of those remaining to June. Of those apples still in his bag, he gave the shiniest one to his teacher. How many apples did Jack have then?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(7\\)",
    "B": "\\(63\\)",
    "C": "\\(65\\)",
    "D": "\\(71\\)",
    "E": "\\(111\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Since \\(25\\%=\\frac14\\), Jill buys \\(\\frac14\\times128=32\\) apples, leaving \\(128-32=96\\). June’s purchase is one quarter of these remaining \\(96\\) apples, so she buys \\(\\frac14\\times96=24\\), leaving \\(96-24=72\\). After Jack gives his teacher one apple, he has\n\\[\n72-1=71\n\\]\napples. The answer is \\(71\\), choice D.",
